 ## Overview
-Analytic Voxelization converts parametrically defined continuous geometric objects ($Q_c$) into digital object representations ($D_p$) defined on a 3D grid [S1]. Unlike binary voxelization which assigns an all-or-none membership value, this method assigns each voxel a membership value in the range $[0, 1]$ reflecting the fraction of the total voxel volume occupied by the continuous object [S1]. Builds on [Analytic and Algebraic Methods](7913-analytic-and-algebraic-methods.md).
