 ## Background
-The concept of digitizing continuous parametric objects into digital representations was introduced in the context of imaging transforms for visualizing surfaces and volumes [S1]. The work by Upad and Goncalves highlights the need for such digitization in applications like prosthesis design and radiation therapy planning [S1]. The method is part of a broader family of analytic and algebraic voxelization techniques that aim to preserve geometric information during the discretization process [G].
